**Narrow `evidence` to `string` before `JSON.parse` in the address-local test.**

`Finding.evidence` is `string | string[] | undefined`. The non-null assertion removes `undefined` but keeps `string[]`, and `JSON.parse` accepts only `string`. This is a strict type error at `test/ops/review/address-local.test.ts:622`. The root `tsconfig.json` includes `test`, and the typecheck ratchet fails when the error count exceeds the committed baseline. Replace the assertion with a runtime guard:

<details>
<summary>Suggested fix</summary>

```diff
-    expect(JSON.parse(report.findings[0]!.evidence!)).toEqual(retained);
+    const evidence = report.findings[0]!.evidence;
+    if (typeof evidence !== 'string') throw new Error('expected serialized failed-attempt evidence');
+    expect(JSON.parse(evidence)).toEqual(retained);
```

</details>
